title "Three ways a layout is refused"
layout layered dir=down
page a4 portrait margin=1cm

style stat color=#1565C0
style search color=#6A1B9A
style after color=#2E7D32

node src "Source with require, align, group"

node classes "E0008: merge classes" .stat
| before any search, each axis on its own
| top, bottom, row merge nodes vertically;
| left, right, column horizontally (union-find)
node cycle "Find a contradiction" .stat
| an ordering inside one class, or a cycle of orderings
| between classes, can never hold: boxes have positive size,
| gaps are non-negative
| BFS over (node, used-an-ordering) states, so the reported
| cycle is short and every constraint on it gets a label

node grid "E0110: search fails" .search
| geometry: sizes, page bounds, candidate positions
node core "Minimal core" .search
| QuickXplain: drop any one listed require and the rest hold
| groups appear in it like requires
node proved "Proved or budgeted?" .search
| proved for every candidate position this layout considers,
| or a probe ran out of checks: the core may be an artifact
| of --budget, and a larger one is suggested
| no layout fits makes the same distinction
node help "Help printed" .search
| remove one, turn it into prefer, or use a larger page;
| the default 7pt floor can be lowered with font

node check "Checker" .after
| an independent pass over the finished drawing
| re-derives overlap, edges through nodes, crossings,
| off page, text overflow, font size: E0101-E0107
| any error stops output; --force writes it anyway

src -> classes, grid, check
classes -> cycle
grid -> core -> proved -> help
